  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14201070/assets/4c8bc8341b9619e9fddb151b02d2d859fab801fe35114de6b2ce6d09045fff11.png)\n\nFor the quadrilateral above, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $B$ is ${180}^{∘}-(4x+{18}^{∘})={162}^{∘}-4x.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x+{15}^{∘})+({162}^{∘}-4x)+(4x-{2}^{∘})+(3x+{1}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{176}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={184}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={23}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠C$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{2}^{∘} & =4({23}^{∘})-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={92}^{∘}-{2}^{∘} \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
